## Specification structure (`specifications/`)

This project follows the spec process documented in
`.harness/pack/specifications/README.md` and
`.harness/pack/specifications/conventions.md`, indexed for this project by
`specifications/README.md`. See those files for document types, ownership
rules, numbering conventions, and the canonical document flow:

```
research → spec → design-spec → ADR → epics-and-tasks → implementation
```

Each gate must produce its artifact before the next begins. ADRs come
in two flavours:

- **Feature-scoped** (`ADR-NNN-<feature>.md`) — uses
  `.harness/pack/specifications/adr-feature.template.md`.
- **Epic-scoped** (`ADR-EXX-<feature>.md`) — uses
  `.harness/pack/specifications/adr-epic.template.md`. Includes the
  file-level plan and public interface contract that the implementer and
  testwriter work against.

Status values across every spec doc: `Draft | In Review | Accepted |
Superseded`. Open questions are numbered `Q-N` and keep that ID when
they move to the Resolved Decisions table.

Current counter state (do not reuse these numbers):

| Counter | Last used | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Epic | E-00 | — |
| Task | T-0000 | — |
| User story | US-00 | — |
| ADR | ADR-000 | Epic-scoped ADRs use the `ADR-EXX` form and do not consume the feature-scoped counter |

