## Agents and agent teams

Ten sub-agent definitions live in `.claude/agents/`. Spawn one by name;
each has a non-overlapping write boundary, and `architect`, `reviewer` and
`securityreviewer` are read-only.

| Agent | Spawn it to |
|---|---|
| `researcher` | investigate an unfamiliar technology and return sourced findings |
| `specwriter` | turn a brief into a functional specification |
| `designer` | write the UI/UX design spec for a feature with an interface |
| `copywriter` | write user-facing text against `copy/tone-of-voice.md` |
| `architect` | validate a spec and produce the ADR that gates implementation |
| `securityreviewer` | check security requirements at the ADR gate and the code at the review gate |
| `implementer` | write code and unit tests from a spec plus a PROCEED-stamped ADR |
| `testwriter` | write integration and acceptance tests against the spec |
| `reviewer` | review code for quality, correctness and security |
| `target-reviewer` | gate a target's readiness before an unsupervised run |

Two team prompts wire them together: `AgentTeams/Specify.md` (brief → a
PROCEED-stamped spec set) and `AgentTeams/Implement.md` (spec set →
shipped code, one epic at a time). The intended flow is the first, then a
human read, then the second.

The file-ownership matrix each team enforces is in
`.harness/pack/agents/README.md`.

