<!-- harness:region id=targets -->

## Autonomous work — targets

Long-running, unsupervised work uses a **target** (`targets/README.md`,
`targets/Run.md`, and the blank contract at
`.harness/pack/targets/target.template.md`): a well-defined,
**measurable** goal the agent works toward on its own and stops at **SUCCESS**
(every verifiable success criterion met) or **ABORT** (a stop condition fired) —
no open-ended "improve X".

- **Launch:** `/target <target-file>` (`.claude/commands/target.md`, which
  follows `targets/Run.md`).
- **Readiness gate:** the `target-reviewer` agent (`.claude/agents/`) validates a
  filled target — criteria verifiable + complete + not gameable, and the
  permission/autonomy envelope sufficient to finish without asking — and returns
  `READY` / `NEEDS-CORRECTION` **before** any work starts. No run starts on a
  failed gate.
- **Instances:** filled targets and their work logs are project content — keep
  them in `targets/` (or `specifications/{{version}}/`), not `.claude/`.

See `targets/README.md` for the lifecycle.

<!-- harness:end -->
